# Changelog Rule

Every user message that results in one or more project modifications must create **one** new entry in root `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Entry contents

Each entry must include:

- The new version number
- The date
- The timestamp using a 12-hour clock with AM/PM
- What was changed
- Why the change was made

## Template

```markdown
## Version XX.XX.XX
Date: MM/DD/YYYY
Time: H:MM AM/PM

### Changes
- ...

### Reason
...
```

## Rules

- Multiple modifications in one user message → **one** changelog entry only.
- Place new entries **above** older ones (newest first).
- Never remove, overwrite, or alter previous entries unless the user specifically requests it.
- Changelog version must always match the current project version in `VERSION`.
- Each new entry raises the version by exactly 00.00.01 (00.00.34 -> 00.00.35 -> 00.00.36 ...), whatever the size of the change. When the last part passes 99 it rolls over (00.00.99 -> 00.01.00).
- Don't renumber old entries unless the user asks (done once, at 00.00.34, at the user's request).
